      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T02:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Add something)\n\nI think previous implementation tries to leverage deviceLostCallback to check the status but Kai pointed out that it might have timing gap between real lost and callback invocation. So we need to check dawn native device status in gpu process and get the status immediately.",
      "parentUuid": "25aa9713_eaa5df9e",
      "revId": "0122c5c3aa0a044dd07dfba50fdd5c49c9bd7de9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "341d77bb_41884f06",
        "filename": "include/dawn/native/DawnNative.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T02:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eAn alternative is https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.h;drc\u003d5e74ac5d42bce00b534d992272e7fa09b53b300f;l\u003d99 though we also would like to remove it eventually.\n\nI don\u0027t know how could we use it in our scenario. Maybe you have some ideas? We wants to:\n- Issuing a clear/draw op using other context when dawn device is lost.\n\nWe find a possible valid context from webgpu_decoder but it requires the API in this CL. Or do you think using \"  gl::GLApi* const api \u003d gl::g_current_gl_context;\" in every shared image backend to do this and using SharedResourceMemory::APIIsDeviceLost() work?",
      "parentUuid": "b67ab718_f8987e26",
      "revId": "0122c5c3aa0a044dd07dfba50fdd5c49c9bd7de9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5006b49_21f4d3c9",
        "filename": "include/dawn/native/DawnNative.h",
