      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T11:48:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I followed the last comment, what does GL have to do with this? In every SIB if we have a Dawn STM then we should be able to check with STM::IsDeviceLost(). But if for some reason that\u0027s not possible I think it is fine to add this API (and add it to webgpu.h eventually imho)",
      "parentUuid": "341d77bb_41884f06",
      "revId": "0122c5c3aa0a044dd07dfba50fdd5c49c9bd7de9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa10f6e7_951ed0a7",
        "filename": "include/dawn/native/DawnNative.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-12T00:56:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The last comments is not about detecting Dawn device status :)\n\nI want to describe why we need this API instead of using https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/SharedResourceMemory.h;drc\u003d5e74ac5d42bce00b534d992272e7fa09b53b300f;l\u003d99.\n\nBecause we need an alternative context to clear the SI (if dawn device is lost). So there are two optional, from webgpu_decoder_impl.cc with shared_context or dive into each si backing with gl::g_current_gl_context",
      "parentUuid": "d5006b49_21f4d3c9",
      "revId": "0122c5c3aa0a044dd07dfba50fdd5c49c9bd7de9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
